## Run 1 — INVALIDATED (corpus granularity defect, diagnosed mid-run)

Index task13-guru45001-kb (corpus v1, 31 docs, depth-3 granularity).
Result: mean 0.7533, retrieval recall 0.7333, $0.0522.
DIAGNOSIS (at 27/50, before final score known — anti-cherry-pick): every
zero-score task expected DEPTH-4 sub-clauses (6.1.2.1/.2/.3, 8.1.4.2/.3);
corpus v1 merged those families into 6.1.2 and 8.1.4 docs, so the model could
never see or cite depth-4 numbers. Score == retrieval recall exactly — a
corpus/harness artifact, not a model failure. 16/50 tasks expect depth-4.
Raw outputs preserved: runs/task13-kimi-run1-corpusv1-INVALID/.

## Corpus v2 fix

6.1.2 split into 6.1.2.1 (hazard identification), 6.1.2.2 (OH&S risk
assessment), 6.1.2.3 (OH&S opportunities); 8.1.4 split into 8.1.4.1
(procurement), 8.1.4.2 (contractors), 8.1.4.3 (outsourcing). 35 docs total.
Coverage check vs eval set: zero missing clause refs (bare '6.2' expectation
satisfied by substring of 6.2.1/6.2.2 citations). Seeded task13-guru45001-kb2,
template check PASS, 35/35 visible.

## Run 2 — VALID RESULT

Index task13-guru45001-kb2 (corpus v2). runs/task13-kimi-run2-corpusv2/ + summary.json:

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Mean clause-citation | **0.9433** |
| Bar | 0.85 |
| **Outcome** | **PASS — Outcome A** |
| Mean retrieval recall (expected clause in top-5) | 0.9233 |
| Retrieval cold starts | 0 |
| Cost | $0.0553 |

Residual misses (5 tasks, scores 0.33–0.50): ALL multi-clause tasks where
score == retrieval recall — kimi correctly cited every clause whose doc reached
top-5; the residual is retrieval breadth (topK=5 vs 2–3 expected clauses), not
model mis-citation. Zero cases of the model citing wrongly from retrieved docs.
Grounding hypothesis from spec-30 CONFIRMED: 0.843 ungrounded → 0.9433 grounded.

